  "descriptionMarkdown": "\n**Early-game Vulcanus Starter Base – Fully Automated, Nauvis Tech Only, Easy to Upgrade**\n\nThis blueprint is designed to make the early game on Vulcanus smoother, especially for players who find the start slow or tedious. It’s a complete, self-sustaining factory you can drop early in the game and upgrade later when you're ready.\n\n### Key Features:\n\n* **Self-bootstrapped power**\n  Solar panels power the chemical plants that produce steam, which then powers the main factory—no manual setup needed beyond input connections.\n\n* **Handles all early-game resources**\n  Automatically consumes the extra ores collected from volcanic rocks and chimney vents using buffer chests.\n\n* **Foundry production included**\n  Produces the first foundry using Nauvis tech and switches to Vulcanus tech automatically using a circuit trick. No manual switching needed.\n\n* **Uses only Nauvis tech**\n  Built entirely with red belts, assembler 3, and modules 2, so it’s placeable early without needing advanced research.\n\n* **Foundries build themselves**\n  Even though the layout includes foundries and Vulcanus tech, it can be placed right away—just add construction bots to the logistics network.\n\n* **Mini mall for ammo and essentials**\n  Includes ammo production and early logistics support to help push through worm territory.\n\n* **125 SPM + small rocket parts production**\n  Supports steady early research and unlock progression.\n\n* **Easy to upgrade**\n  Layout is designed for seamless upgrades—belts, assemblers, and modules can be upgraded without rebuilding.\n\n* **Fulgora-ready circuit section**\n  Circuit production starts with Nauvis tech but has enough space to replace it with Fulgora circuits later.\n\n### To start:\n\n1. You don’t need foundries—this factory builds them automatically.\n2. Connect input materials; the factory will power up and start on its own.\n3. Add some logistics and construction bots to the network.\n\n### Updates\n30/Sep/2025:\n- Switched from AM2 to AM3 with more productivity modules - on one hand it increase the factory's cost, but on the other hand - until coal liquefaction is researched we are very slow on production and the additional productivity modules adds an important boost\n- Changed logic to keep much less heavy and light oil before using it - reduced from 30,000 to 3,000.\n- Increased the production of heavy oil in the simple coal liquefaction refinery. Thanks go to **Jose Maria Bastida** for pointing the problem to me\n\n18/Jul/2025: \n- Bug fixes and small improvements",
